.page fold 1 wrap long lines

# SYNOPSIS
*fold* [*-s*] [*-w* _N_] [_FILE_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`fold` breaks every input line that is longer than _N_ bytes (80 by default) into several output lines.

# OPTIONS
@ *-w* _N_
    The width at which to break.
@ *-s*
    Break at the last space before the limit when there is one, so words are not cut in half.

# EXAMPLES
    fold -s -w 60 article.txt
    echo "a very long line indeed" | fold -w 10

# NOTES
`fold` counts bytes, not characters, so UTF-8 text may be cut in the middle of a character.

# SEE ALSO
cut(1), nl(1), patchouli-pager(1)
